  "selected_statement": {
    "theorem": "1-1-finite-crossover",
    "doi": "10.5802/jep.207"
  },
  "closure": "Full author mathematical body retained. Complete finite-crossover part of Theorem1 and all new exact enumeration/core-kernel/contraction/loop-ratio/tail core are retained. Original illustration assets are retained separately; every statement/proof formula and prose line remains editable. Later divergent-crossover and scaling-limit claims are unselected context.",
  "current_difficulty_reason": "A pointwise enumeration ratio is insufficient to determine the defect law because mass could escape through arbitrarily large defects. Sections2–3 prove the exact core-kernel enumeration and uniform near-trivalent contraction ratios, transferring loop controls through Catalan-weighted forests. Section4 combines those new estimates with a uniform factorial tail to normalize the finite-crossover Poisson law, so its difficulty is not the final ratio-to-Poisson calculation alone.",
  "editorial_changes": [
    "Independent article layout and explicit source, scope and difficulty boundary",
    "Bibliography restored from exact matching cached publisher HTML with native math annotations",
    "Necessary native macro definitions retained; only publisher typography commands mapped to ordinary article equivalents",
    "Selected finite-crossover proof ends at source972; later divergent-crossover negative-deviation omission is unselected and is not claimed complete.",
    "Eight original raster illustration assets recovered with pixel-exact soft-mask composition where present; five flattened-vector original diagram viewports retain byte-exact full-page decoded content and exact inspected clip rectangles. Captions/explanatory/proof mathematics remain native editable TeX.",
    "The first contour viewport visibly cut the left minus sign in the original -2c label; viewport widened to include the complete original label, preserving page drawing bytes. Prior clip/PDF/build evidence retained."
  ],
